  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1057 PM CDT Mon Jun 29 2026\n\nMiddle Tennessee won't see appreciable rain chances until\nThursday, by which time the ridge will start to flatten out and we\ncan perhaps expect to get diurnal convection mainly during peak- \nheating hours. Temperatures and heat indices will start to back\noff a little starting on Saturday, at least enough so that no\nadvisories would be needed. Also, rain chances will pick up a\nlittle bit over the weekend as a surface boundary and upper trough\nmight actually slip through. Temperatures next week look to stay\ncloser to seasonal normals, which would certainly bring some \nrelief following this week's hot weather.",
